WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
See in Pac-Man, you have this little character.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.950
It goes around, finds these pebbles, and the pebbles fit right into it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.950
Well a lot of illustrations that you will find of enzymes happen to look, to us, a lot like Pac-Man.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.950
I remember P for Pac-Man and P for protein.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.950
Most enzymes are proteins.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.950
In the game we mentioned these little pebbles that Pac-Man goes after.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.950
Well enzymes have a specifically shaped area, called an active site, where items can bind, called substrates.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.950
It’s very specific binding because the active site is specifically shaped for the substrate that binds there.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.950
Very specific.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.950
So what happens when substrates bind an enzyme?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.950
Well usually the substrate is held there with weak bonds because it’s not going to stay there forever.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:01.950
Something called induced fit will happen which means the active site can change its shape even more to bind that substrate perfectly.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.950
Like… an enzyme-substrate hug.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.950
The enzyme can either build up or break down the substrates that specifically bind to it, and we call the resulting item the product.
